    "kind": "certification",
    "proves": "Verify that all core services accept mTLS connections with the cluster CA.\n\nUses openssl s_client to perform a TLS handshake against each service's\ngRPC endpoint. A successful handshake proves:\n  - The service is listening on the expected port\n  - The service cert is trusted by the cluster CA\n  - The service accepts client certs issued by the cluster CA\n  - The TLS chain is valid end-to-end\n\nThis is the network-level security proof that the mTLS mesh is operational.\nIt does NOT test authorization (that's authz-enforcement) \u2014 only transport security.\n\nServices tested (from service matrix):\n  - authentication   10.10.0.11:10005\n  - rbac             10.10.0.11:10004\n  - workflow         10.10.0.11:10220\n  - event            10.10.0.11:10000\n  - repository       10.10.0.12:10009",
